course: dictionary
lesson: 8716
title: Sensitive: five meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. «Sensitive» is a good example. The sentence around it tells you which meaning the author means. «Mia has sensitive teeth, so cold drinks hurt her.» Here sensitive means easily harmed by something. The clue is the cold drinks that hurt.
explain: «Sam went quiet after the class laughed at his drawing. He is very sensitive.» Sensitive here means easily hurt or upset by what others say or do. Another clue is the word quiet, which shows Sam has been upset.
explain: «The scales are so sensitive they weigh a single grain of salt.» Here sensitive means able to notice very small changes. Try the swap test: put «easily hurt» into the sentence and it does not make sense. So this is not the meaning.
fact: «Sensitive» is an adjective. It can change to «more sensitive» and «most sensitive».
fact: «Sensitive» can mean easily hurt or upset by what others say or do, or easily affected by something, like sensitive skin.
fact: «Sensitive» can also mean able to notice very small changes, like a sensitive instrument, or understanding other people's feelings.
fact: In French, «sensible» means sensitive. English «sensible» means wise and practical, so do not mix them up.
fact: Secret or private information that needs care is also called sensitive, such as passwords.
exercise: «Dogs and cats hide on fireworks night because their hearing is far more sensitive than ours.» What does sensitive mean here? | Slow to move | Easily upset by people's words | Cold to the touch | *Able to notice very small sounds
exercise: Sam's friend laughed at his new haircut, and Sam went quiet and sad. Which word describes Sam? | Sensible | Sensitive scales | *Sensitive, easily hurt by what others say | Sensitive
exercise: Which of these is sensitive information you should never share online? | The name of your pet | A photo of a sunset | Your favourite film | *Your password
test: Mia has sensitive teeth, so cold drinks hurt her. What does sensitive mean here? | Happy and calm | Sensible and wise | Able to hear very far | *Easily affected or harmed by something
test: English «sensible» means wise and practical. What does French «sensible» mean? | Wise and practical | Loud and busy | *Sensitive, easily upset or touched | Quick and clever
exam: «Elephants throw mud over their backs, which protects their sensitive skin from sunburn and biting insects.» What does sensitive skin mean here? | Skin that is thick and hard | *Skin that is easily harmed by the sun and insects | Skin that is wet and cold | Skin that is shiny and smooth
